Scope: Gemini explicit cachedContent resource (separate from request-level
prompt caching covered by Langertha::PromptCache). cachedContent is a
server-side managed cache of input context with its own lifecycle:
  - create via POST /v1beta/cachedContents (long-lived resource)
  - reference in generateContent body via cachedContent field
  - TTL + expiration managed via separate REST endpoints
  - usage_metadata.cached_content_token_count surfaces cached vs fresh
Source: ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/caching

Proposed sub-tickets:
  22a — research: map cachedContents REST endpoints, fields, expiry
        semantics; cross-check current ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs
  22b — value object: Langertha::CachedContent (id, model, ttl,
        system_instruction)
  22c — role: Langertha::Role::CachedContent lifecycle wrapper
        (create/get/list/update/delete; expiry tracking)
  22d — wire: Langertha::Engine::Gemini request body takes optional
        cachedContent => {name=>...}; emits cachedContents as body part
        when set; update role/engine_capabilities to advertise
        cachedContent on Gemini 2.5+ and Gemini 3
  22e — telemetry: Langertha::Response.usage surface adds
        cached_content_token_count when present in response
  22f — tests (offline + live); offline wire replay using saved
        generateContent response fixture; live gated on
        TEST_LANGERTHA_GEMINI_API_KEY

Adjacent (NOT in #22, separate ticket if pursued):
  - Anthropic prompt caching (covered by Langertha::PromptCache per ADR 0009)
  - OpenAI automatic caching (no explicit interface)
